WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.100
From a Law &amp; Order: SVU star's collapsed&nbsp;
lung to a British stuntman's paralysis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.447
from the waist down, these are some of the&nbsp;
small screen's ugliest on-set injuries.

00:00:10.149 --> 00:00:13.920
The Good Wife is a courtroom drama that&nbsp;
debuted in 2009. The show's creators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.120
Michelle and Robert King, were inspired&nbsp;
after seeing many cases of wives standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.260
by their disgraced politician husbands after&nbsp;
they confessed to an affair. Surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.200
a courtroom drama made the cut for&nbsp;
a list like this. Nevertheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.260
stunts aren't the only thing that&nbsp;
could go wrong on a television set.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.160
Kristin Chenoweth was on the set of The Good&nbsp;
Wife for an outdoor sequence when a piece of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.880
lighting production equipment fell on her&nbsp;
head. During an appearance on Andy Cohen's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.900
Watch What Happens Live, the actress said the&nbsp;
terrifying event "practically killed" her.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.400
Chenoweth also revealed in the interview that&nbsp;
she fell unconscious instantly and woke up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.140
a hospital bed. The horrific accident left her&nbsp;
with a 7-inch skull fracture and broken teeth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.760
among other injuries. The actor's doctor told her&nbsp;
that if it hadn't been for her hair extensions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.700
she would have died that day since&nbsp;
they held the hairline fracture on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.180
her head together. She told Cohen that&nbsp;
she has "long standing injuries" as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.080
result of the event and regrets not&nbsp;
suing CBS over it. She explained:

00:01:04.366 --> 00:01:08.266
"I didn't do it out of fear and anxiety."

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.500
Netflix had its work cut out for it when adapting&nbsp;
Cowboy Bebop, one of the best anime shows of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.300
time. The beloved sci-fi series has a dedicated&nbsp;
cult following, so getting the right cast was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:23.220
always going to be vital. John Cho was ultimately&nbsp;
cast as protagonist Spike Spiegel. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:28.740
Cho hurt his knee during the filming of the highly&nbsp;
anticipated show, tearing his ACL. The ACL tissue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.820
is the muscle that links the thigh bone to&nbsp;
the shin and is commonly torn in athletes.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.760
Cho's recuperation from his ACL injury took a toll&nbsp;
on him not only physically but also mentally. In a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.180
promotional interview for the series, the&nbsp;
actor told Vulture that he was concerned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.980
about his extended time off, primarily for how it&nbsp;
affected the show's production. He told Vulture:

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.280
"I felt very guilty that I had let&nbsp;
the production down, and my cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.060
and the crew in New Zealand that had had&nbsp;
a job, and then they didn't the next day."

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.800
It's always a daunting task for television&nbsp;
executives to develop a police procedural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.940
that stands out from the crowd. The method&nbsp;
9-1-1 adopted was depending on the sheer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.560
star power of actors like Angela Bassett and&nbsp;
Peter Krause while bringing in talented guest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.900
stars to support them. UFC and WWE star&nbsp;
Ronda Rousey was one such guest. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.920
Rousey's guest appearance did not go as&nbsp;
planned, as she sustained a gruesome injury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.120
while filming. Rousey described the event in&nbsp;
a social media post, revealing that on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.800
very first take on a specific day, her finger&nbsp;
was crushed by a boat door and nearly severed.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:30.250
"Yeah, I looked down and my&nbsp;
finger was barely hanging on."

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.140
While showing a picture of the injury, Rousey&nbsp;
wrote in the caption of an Instagram post:

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.520
"I thought I just jammed my fingers so I finished&nbsp;
the take before looking [...] [A]fter a break in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.540
the action I told our director the situation&nbsp;
and was rushed via ambulance to the hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.500
where they promptly reattached my bone&nbsp;
and tendon with a plate and screws."

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.680
Rousey went on to praise the medical&nbsp;
team that worked on her finger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.580
revealing that 50% of normal motion had&nbsp;
returned within three days of her surgery.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:03:00.180
Prison Break debuted in 2005 and quickly became&nbsp;
a cultural phenomenon. The drama morphed into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.600
sort of travel show with the main characters&nbsp;
being pulled into an ever-growing government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:07.800
conspiracy that forces them into different&nbsp;
prisons all over the world. In Season 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.900
a conspiracy leads the gang to Yemen. During the&nbsp;
shooting of an action scene, an iron bar fell from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.640
20 feet and struck Dominic Purcell on the head,&nbsp;
leaving him seriously injured. He told Deadline:

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.840
"I dropped to my knees, and I was in shock.&nbsp;
I'm just leaning over and the blood is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.620
pouring out like a shower, and my stunt guy&nbsp;
came up beside me [...] And he said, 'Your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.640
head's split right open, I can see your skull,&nbsp;
your nose is on the other side of your face.'"

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.420
Because they were shooting in a remote part&nbsp;
of Morocco, the kind of medical assistance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.020
he needed wasn't immediately available.&nbsp;
When the doctors at the local clinic he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.820
was taken to started arguing amongst themselves,&nbsp;
he walked out. As Purcell explained to Deadline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.060
his girlfriend then "took control"&nbsp;
of the situation. He told the outlet:

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.180
"[She] poured alcohol on my&nbsp;
head, and wrapped me up in gauze,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.900
and then Fox got a helicopter and they&nbsp;
flew me out from Ouarzazate to Casablanca."

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.600
He was taken to a renowned&nbsp;
plastic surgeon in Casablanca,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.560
who was able to fix him up. The actor was&nbsp;
lucky to escape the ordeal with his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.200
but he still has visible scars&nbsp;
on his scalp to this day.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:06.550
"Um, was uh, that's where the&nbsp;
white of my skull was showing."

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:11.280
Mariska Hargitay has starred as Olivia&nbsp;
Benson in over 500 episodes of Law &amp; Order:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.240
Special Victims Unit. Not every episode&nbsp;
has been a joy to film for Hargitay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:19.260
but one led to a very serious injury. She&nbsp;
recalled during an interview with Redbook:

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:23.160
"I was doing a stunt chasing a bad&nbsp;
guy. I jumped and landed on pads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.500
but on the second take something happened — I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.800
landed wrong. I got up and felt that&nbsp;
something inside was not quite right."

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.580
The actor shrugged it off as a muscle injury,&nbsp;
and she seemed to get better. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.660
three months later, she was walking on the&nbsp;
beach when she suddenly experienced an intense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.280
stabbing pain in her chest and was unable to&nbsp;
catch her breath. The actress revealed to Redbook:

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.840
"They took an X-ray and found that my&nbsp;
right lung was 50% collapsed. I began to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.980
panic. I was so scared. I had a procedure&nbsp;
hoping to stave off more serious surgery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.340
but it didn't work, and I ended up&nbsp;
in surgery about two weeks later."

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.180
Hargitay was told that the repaired lung&nbsp;
was now healthier than her other lung,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.840
but that there was still about a one in&nbsp;
1,000 chance that it would collapse again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:04.380
Despite those seemingly favorable&nbsp;
odds, however, her lung collapsed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:08.220
once again. However, she isn't bitter&nbsp;
about it. The actress told Redbook:

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.960
"I get to be the one in 1,000 in so many&nbsp;
positive ways, it balances out. I have so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:16.560
many blessings, and I've learned from&nbsp;
all of my experiences and my losses."

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.080
As Stephen Amell's tenure on Arrow ended, fans&nbsp;
hoped that his next project would capitalize on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.560
his abilities as a physical actor with&nbsp;
considerable dramatic chops. When the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.060
trailer for Heels was released, it promised to&nbsp;
do just that in an inventive way. The show is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.200
about a wrestler in a small town attempting&nbsp;
to build a wrestling dynasty. The nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.860
the show meant that Amell would have to do a&nbsp;
lot of physical stuff, thus putting himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:42.600
in potential danger. It wasn't long before&nbsp;
he picked up a nasty injury. Amell told ABC:

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.500
"I overshot it coast to coast on our first&nbsp;
day of filming wrestling stuff and suffered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.520
a compression fracture. I'm very fortunate and&nbsp;
lucky that it was an injury that sounds scary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.820
but didn't require surgery. [It]&nbsp;
just sort of healed on its own."

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.980
It was a terrifying moment not just for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.280
but for everyone involved in the&nbsp;
production. The actor told ABC:

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.960
"I certainly scared a lot of people."

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.020
Amell developed a huge respect for&nbsp;
professional wrestlers while making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.560
the show. He went on to say that he has&nbsp;
no intention of swapping his comfortable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.800
life as an actor for the grind of the&nbsp;
pro-wrestling circuit anytime soon.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.380
Jackass was once the most contentious show on&nbsp;
television. The show's concept stems back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.100
the 1990s when Johnny Knoxville was trying&nbsp;
to break into Hollywood. He couldn't find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:23.460
acting work so he turned to journalism.&nbsp;
While attempting a career in journalism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.060
Knoxville intended to put together an&nbsp;
article about himself testing self-defense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:31.080
equipment. When Jeff Tremaine, the editor of&nbsp;
a skateboard magazine, heard about the idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:34.920
he asked if he could film it. Knoxville&nbsp;
was introduced to a bunch of like-minded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:39.900
skaters and Jackass was born. The MTV&nbsp;
show went on to be a massive success. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:44.580
with a concept like that, serious injuries are&nbsp;
inevitable. Knoxville told Entertainment Weekly:

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.920
"I have so many doctors in my phone. I have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.920
go for a tune up with one doctor or&nbsp;
another at least once a month now."

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.340
The actor and stuntman sustained&nbsp;
so many injuries during his Jackass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.640
days that it's a wonder he's still&nbsp;
walking. From herniated discs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:00.060
torn tendons to serious concussions,&nbsp;
Knoxville has been through it all.

00:07:00.346 --> 00:07:03.720
"My left eye popped out of its socket and it was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:07.740
the more that I blew the farther it&nbsp;
was coming. So that freaked me out."

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.500
In his Entertainment Weekly&nbsp;
interview, Knoxville admitted:

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.220
"Sometimes after a concussion you get a&nbsp;
little down. But it kind of works itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:18.240
out. I feel like I'm very strong physically&nbsp;
and mentally. I'm very lucky — it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.360
always work out like this for a man who's&nbsp;
had the amount of injuries that I've had."

00:07:21.943 --> 00:07:27.120
Ozzy Osbourne first gained notoriety in the 1970s&nbsp;
as the lead singer of the British rock band Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:32.280
Sabbath. Osbourne's fame went beyond the band as&nbsp;
his antics made him notorious in the tabloids. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:37.080
the early 2000s, MTV capitalized on Osbourne's&nbsp;
celebrity by greenlighting a reality show about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:41.760
him and his family. The Osbournes didn't shy&nbsp;
away from revealing big life events, such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:46.500
Sharon's cancer battle. One such significant event&nbsp;
was the quad bike accident that injured Ozzy.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.760
Osbourne was riding his quad bike on the grounds&nbsp;
of the family's estate in England when he hit some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:55.440
uneven ground and was thrown from the vehicle.&nbsp;
Osbourne's bodyguard Sam Ruston told ABC:

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:59.940
"As the bike's tumbling and he's tumbling, he&nbsp;
actually somehow gets entangled in the bike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:03.900
and he's rolling with the bike. I turned&nbsp;
him over and I put my head on his chest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.300
and I hear no breath, no heartbeat, nothing."

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:10.800
Ruston performed mouth-to-mouth on Osbourne.&nbsp;
When the rocker finally came around, he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:15.180
immediately transported to a hospital. Doctors&nbsp;
found that one of Osbourne's lungs was partially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:19.620
collapsed and several bones were damaged. Eight&nbsp;
of Osbourne's ribs, some of his vertebrae,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:24.120
and his left collarbone were all fractured.&nbsp;
In 2019, he revealed that he was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:28.794
feeling the aftereffects of the accident. In&nbsp;
an interview with SiriusXM, Osbourne revealed:

00:08:28.794 --> 00:08:31.674
"For the last 10 years, I've been&nbsp;
getting electric shocks down my arm."

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:36.180
At this point in history, Simon Cowell's&nbsp;
standing in pop culture is more related to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:40.440
his reputation as a caustic judge on numerous&nbsp;
talent programs than to his actual day job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:45.300
as a record label head. However, few fans are&nbsp;
aware that Cowell himself was once a contestant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.380
on an obscure talent show called Sale of&nbsp;
the Century. His fondness for the format,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:53.880
along with his notion that controversy garners&nbsp;
attention, inspired Cowells to create the Got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.680
Talent franchise. Since then, the Got Talent&nbsp;
franchise has spawned over a hundred spin-offs.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.940
America's Got Talent: Extreme was one&nbsp;
such spin-off. The concept was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:06.060
same as in previous incarnations,&nbsp;
with a combination of the judges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:10.440
host, and viewers voting for their favorite&nbsp;
contestant. The only difference was that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:15.120
version contained daredevil stunts. However,&nbsp;
a horrific accident on the set resulted in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.320
show being suspended indefinitely in 2021,&nbsp;
with Cowell pulling the plug soon after.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:22.260
Jonathan Goodwin, an experienced&nbsp;
British stunt performer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.040
had been in several U.K. television shows&nbsp;
before competing on America's Got Talent:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:30.540
Extreme. He was crushed between two automobiles&nbsp;
after his stunt on America's Got Talent:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:35.040
Extreme went tragically wrong. As a result,&nbsp;
Goodwin was paralyzed from the waist down.

00:09:35.459 --> 00:09:37.740
"The prognosis is that, you know, unless there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:42.000
some sort of amazing thing that happens&nbsp;
that this is me from, from here on out."

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.780
But Goodwin is doing his best to&nbsp;
maintain a positive attitude. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:48.150
an appearance on Loose Women, he had this to say:

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.820
"I wouldn't wish it on anybody but&nbsp;
I think that with all the physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.180
challenges I've had in my life I'm&nbsp;
uniquely adapted to dealing with it."

